  "notes": "Aladin Lite v3 embedded full-viewport. The canvas carries all visual weight: a colour sky survey of Orion B (Alnitak, Flame/Horsehead region) overlaid with hundreds of small red SIMBAD circles, teal diamond YSO candidates, dense orange Gaia squares, lime/purple/orange instrument footprint polygons (CFHT/WIRCam, JWST/NIRCam, VLT/KMOS, MUSE), a translucent orange KMOS coverage MOC, and yellow filled dots for user notes. Chrome is minimal light-grey (#ececec) square-ish buttons with 2px dark borders and 3px radius, monospace text; coordinates show in magenta. Live: layers button opens a 'Stack' panel listing overlays and surveys with eye/settings/delete toggles; clicking a note opens a popover; clicking a catalog source opens a bottom table of attributes. None of these are open in the capture."
